[{:db/id 17592186162063 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f92de356-71ac-5b5e-9291-a3c3ef80d00b" "question-0c6d1e5f-c8c7-58eb-9372-45bad8d48254"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161873 :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P((X,Y)\\in \\{(2,3),(6,1)\\}) & =P((X,Y)=(2,3))+P((X,Y)=(6,1)) \\\\  & =f(2,3)+f(6,1) \\\\  & =0.25+0.3 \\\\  & =0.55.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162074 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-663c80f0-fe5e-502f-84c3-e0164d0d760f" "question-77b7b7f9-a7fd-5ac7-a5d0-130bc06dad6a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161874 :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\cdot Y\\ge 4) & =P((X,Y)\\in \\{(1,4),(2,2),(2,4)\\}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(1,4))+P((X,Y)=(2,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,4)) \\\\  & =f(1,4)+f(2,2)+f(2,4) \\\\  & =0.05+0.25+0.15 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186275145 :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.16$ | $-0.1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.24$ | $0.35$ |\n\nConsider the function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Which of the following conditions is true?\n\nI. $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1$ for all $(x,y)$ in $S$\n\nII. ${\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1$\n\nIII. $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability mass function" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-f92de356-71ac-5b5e-9291-a3c3ef80d00b" :question/id #uuid "f92de356-71ac-5b5e-9291-a3c3ef80d00b" :question/math-academy-id "q-110814" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{a}{3}$ | $a$ | $3a$ |\n| $X=1$ | $4a$ | $\\frac{2a}{3}$ | $\\frac{a}{2}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $a$ | $\\frac{3a}{2}$ | $5a$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above. Find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "The support of $X$ is ${S}_{X}=\\{0,1,2\\},$ the support of $Y$ is ${S}_{Y}=\\{0,1,2\\},$ and therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}=\\{(0,0),(0,1),(0,2),(1,0),(1,1),(1,2),(2,0),(2,1),(2,2)\\}.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y),$ we must have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,0)+f(0,1)+f(0,2)+f(1,0)+f(1,1)+f(1,2)+f(2,0)+f(2,1)+f(2,2) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{a}{3}+a+3a+4a+\\frac{2a}{3}+\\frac{a}{2}+a+\\frac{3a}{2}+5a & =1 \\\\ 17a & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-be04018e-9849-5afe-9540-e80db3c5e1e0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-be04018e-9849-5afe-9540-e80db3c5e1e0" :answer-field/id #uuid "be04018e-9849-5afe-9540-e80db3c5e1e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3d56e76f-6d74-5301-a933-a1c053d1c57f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-28842ea5-4a23-5bc7-aed2-d9be8492202a" "answer-e969a972-3f84-5b88-a3f9-2a70e503ca6a" "answer-3d56e76f-6d74-5301-a933-a1c053d1c57f" "answer-301025df-a886-5236-ad98-3b902e2ea82f" "answer-69907c50-26c1-5b5d-8605-de49a64862bf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28842ea5-4a23-5bc7-aed2-d9be8492202a" :answer/id #uuid "28842ea5-4a23-5bc7-aed2-d9be8492202a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e969a972-3f84-5b88-a3f9-2a70e503ca6a" :answer/id #uuid "e969a972-3f84-5b88-a3f9-2a70e503ca6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d56e76f-6d74-5301-a933-a1c053d1c57f" :answer/id #uuid "3d56e76f-6d74-5301-a933-a1c053d1c57f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-301025df-a886-5236-ad98-3b902e2ea82f" :answer/id #uuid "301025df-a886-5236-ad98-3b902e2ea82f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69907c50-26c1-5b5d-8605-de49a64862bf" :answer/id #uuid "69907c50-26c1-5b5d-8605-de49a64862bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186275141 :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n\nConsider the function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Which of the following conditions is true?\n\nI. $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1$ for all $(x,y)$ in $S$\n\nII. ${\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1$\n\nIII. $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability mass function" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186275144 :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $-0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $-0.3$ |\n\nConsider the function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Which of the following conditions is true?\n\nI. $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1$ for all $(x,y)$ in $S$\n\nII. ${\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1$\n\nIII. $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability mass function" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-0c6d1e5f-c8c7-58eb-9372-45bad8d48254" :question/id #uuid "0c6d1e5f-c8c7-58eb-9372-45bad8d48254" :question/math-academy-id "q-110816" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $a$ | $2a$ | $\\frac{3a}{2}$ | $3a$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above. Find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "The support of $X$ is ${S}_{X}=\\{2\\},$ the support of $Y$ is ${S}_{Y}=\\{0,1,2,3\\},$ and therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}=\\{(2,0),(2,1),(2,2),(2,3)\\}.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y),$ we must have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,0)+f(2,1)+f(2,2)+f(2,3) & =1 \\\\ a+2a+\\frac{3a}{2}+3a & =1 \\\\ \\frac{15a}{2} & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{2}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-64f576c6-2c57-57e4-b5ca-142b4704a492"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-64f576c6-2c57-57e4-b5ca-142b4704a492" :answer-field/id #uuid "64f576c6-2c57-57e4-b5ca-142b4704a492" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-46a9a4d1-f15d-5616-910d-b7da8e99a745" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5bd7862b-aa56-5344-8cc5-e5e15c996f19" "answer-b4066227-6ad9-5005-83a8-f419a328e5af" "answer-46a9a4d1-f15d-5616-910d-b7da8e99a745" "answer-1529ce67-67d0-5c1f-a17d-5ea1c1983d56" "answer-8b11baf7-b6d3-59ae-ad3b-68cd960b0bc2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5bd7862b-aa56-5344-8cc5-e5e15c996f19" :answer/id #uuid "5bd7862b-aa56-5344-8cc5-e5e15c996f19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4066227-6ad9-5005-83a8-f419a328e5af" :answer/id #uuid "b4066227-6ad9-5005-83a8-f419a328e5af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46a9a4d1-f15d-5616-910d-b7da8e99a745" :answer/id #uuid "46a9a4d1-f15d-5616-910d-b7da8e99a745" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1529ce67-67d0-5c1f-a17d-5ea1c1983d56" :answer/id #uuid "1529ce67-67d0-5c1f-a17d-5ea1c1983d56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b11baf7-b6d3-59ae-ad3b-68cd960b0bc2" :answer/id #uuid "8b11baf7-b6d3-59ae-ad3b-68cd960b0bc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247180 :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n\nCompute $P((X,Y)\\in \\{(1,0),(1,2),(2,1),(3,2)\\})$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P((X,Y)\\in \\{(1,0),(1,2),(2,1),(3,2)\\}) & =P((X,Y)=(1,0)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(1,2)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(2,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(3,2)) \\\\  & =f(1,0)+f(1,2)+f(2,1)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =0.05+0.25+0.05+0.05 \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247181 :question/problem "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.35$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P((X,Y)\\in \\{(3,1),(3,2),(3,3)\\})$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P((X,Y)\\in \\{(3,1),(3,2),(3,3)\\}) & =P((X,Y)=(3,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(3,2)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(3,3)) \\\\  & =f(3,1)+f(3,2)+f(3,3) \\\\  & =0.05+0.05+0.1 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-663c80f0-fe5e-502f-84c3-e0164d0d760f" :question/id #uuid "663c80f0-fe5e-502f-84c3-e0164d0d760f" :question/math-academy-id "q-111038" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P(X>0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,Y<2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,Y<2) & =P((X,Y)\\in \\{(1,0),(1,1),(2,0),(2,1)\\}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(1,0))+P((X,Y)=(1,1)) \\\\  & \\,+P((X,Y)=(2,0))+P((X,Y)=(2,1)) \\\\  & =f(1,0)+f(1,1)+f(2,0)+f(2,1) \\\\  & =0.1+0.05+0.15+0.05 \\\\  & =0.35.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e5967368-9c1c-5296-b137-b9913b855878"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e5967368-9c1c-5296-b137-b9913b855878" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5967368-9c1c-5296-b137-b9913b855878" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d0617c28-cbaa-5033-983d-a5bdacd2314a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-170857b0-1781-50ab-a9f3-dac4f2f65bb0" "answer-a7273bb7-d576-55b4-9276-ba60e8a043b2" "answer-d0617c28-cbaa-5033-983d-a5bdacd2314a" "answer-9aee7b06-c6c8-5ba3-b01b-4a684f1c6a98" "answer-35532208-e23a-5095-9966-0c7fc84450af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-170857b0-1781-50ab-a9f3-dac4f2f65bb0" :answer/id #uuid "170857b0-1781-50ab-a9f3-dac4f2f65bb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7273bb7-d576-55b4-9276-ba60e8a043b2" :answer/id #uuid "a7273bb7-d576-55b4-9276-ba60e8a043b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0617c28-cbaa-5033-983d-a5bdacd2314a" :answer/id #uuid "d0617c28-cbaa-5033-983d-a5bdacd2314a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9aee7b06-c6c8-5ba3-b01b-4a684f1c6a98" :answer/id #uuid "9aee7b06-c6c8-5ba3-b01b-4a684f1c6a98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35532208-e23a-5095-9966-0c7fc84450af" :answer/id #uuid "35532208-e23a-5095-9966-0c7fc84450af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162283 :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=6) & =P((X,Y)\\in \\{(1,2),(1,4),(1,6),(2,6)\\}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(1,2))+P((X,Y)=(1,4)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(1,6))+P((X,Y)=(2,6)) \\\\  & =f(1,2)+f(1,4)+f(1,6)+f(2,6) \\\\  & =0.1+0.25+0.25+0.2 \\\\  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-77b7b7f9-a7fd-5ac7-a5d0-130bc06dad6a" :question/id #uuid "77b7b7f9-a7fd-5ac7-a5d0-130bc06dad6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-111035" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nCompute $P(0<Y<2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<Y<2) & =P(Y=1) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)\\in \\{(0,1),(1,1)\\}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(0,1))+P((X,Y)=(1,1)) \\\\  & =f(0,1)+f(1,1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8bfda3ee-73dd-52a0-96d8-63ac91641355"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8bfda3ee-73dd-52a0-96d8-63ac91641355" :answer-field/id #uuid "8bfda3ee-73dd-52a0-96d8-63ac91641355" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b5213fcd-3d80-5a1d-a4e1-5acb2f322104" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0ecbcc89-8b20-5446-8735-5273eb0286fc" "answer-7040bcd7-a549-5c5b-8285-0ee8b9e0078e" "answer-9bd56b69-6cc9-5be6-8903-074d6e9c8049" "answer-b5213fcd-3d80-5a1d-a4e1-5acb2f322104" "answer-04fbecf1-c27f-59ee-850b-c3f175aae366"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ecbcc89-8b20-5446-8735-5273eb0286fc" :answer/id #uuid "0ecbcc89-8b20-5446-8735-5273eb0286fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7040bcd7-a549-5c5b-8285-0ee8b9e0078e" :answer/id #uuid "7040bcd7-a549-5c5b-8285-0ee8b9e0078e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bd56b69-6cc9-5be6-8903-074d6e9c8049" :answer/id #uuid "9bd56b69-6cc9-5be6-8903-074d6e9c8049" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5213fcd-3d80-5a1d-a4e1-5acb2f322104" :answer/id #uuid "b5213fcd-3d80-5a1d-a4e1-5acb2f322104" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04fbecf1-c27f-59ee-850b-c3f175aae366" :answer/id #uuid "04fbecf1-c27f-59ee-850b-c3f175aae366" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247203 :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=0) & =P((X,Y)\\in \\{(0,0),(1,0),(2,0),(2,1),(2,2)\\}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(0,0))+P((X,Y)=(1,0))+P((X,Y)=(2,0)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(2,1))+P((X,Y)=(2,2)) \\\\  & =f(0,0)+f(1,0)+f(2,0)+f(2,1)+f(2,2) \\\\  & =0.15+0.1+0.05+0.1+0.1 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163262 :tutorial/content "We often want to know if there is a relationship between two random variables. For this reason, we wish to formulate the idea of a joint probability distribution.\n\nTo introduce this concept, suppose the random variable $X$ represents the number of heads obtained when a fair coin is flipped. The support of $X,$ denoted $S_X,$ consists of all possible values of $X$ and in this case is given by\n\n$$\nS_X = \\{0,1\\}.\n$$\n\nNow suppose that the random variable $Y$ represents the result of rolling a fair tetrahedral die. Then the support of $Y,$ denoted $S_Y,$ is\n\n$$\nS_Y = \\{1,2,3,4\\}.\n$$\n\nThe **joint support** of $X$ and $Y,$ denoted $S,$ consists of all possible pairs $(x,y)$ such that $x$ is a possible outcome for $X$ and $y$ is a possible outcome for $Y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/34/34a8b2e96a6ef41d66c441aebe08d204a0bc84b210f8de04c836907f0afd9d29.svg)\n\nNote that $S_X\\times S_Y$ is the cartesian product of $S_X$ and $S_Y.$\n\nLet's assume that the flipping of the coin and rolling of the die are independent. Then, for any $x \\in X$ and any $y \\in Y,$ we have that\n\n$$\nP(X=x\\:\\textrm{and}\\:Y=y) = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{4} = \\dfrac{1}{8}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe **joint probability mass function** of $X$ and $Y,$ denoted $f(x,y),$ can be represented by the following table:\n\n| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ |\n\n \n\nSimilar to the case of single random variables, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y) = P(X=x\\:\\textrm{ and }\\:Y=y).\n$$\n\nGoing forward, we will use the shorthand notation $P(X=x, Y=y)$ to mean $P(X=x\\:\\textrm{ and }\\:Y=y).$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162162 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
